  "notes": "Includes a printed inner sleeve with lyrics, credits and thank yous on one side and a photo of Tracy Chapman on the other.\n\n\"SP\" in label matrix and \"E A S T\" embossed on side B label denote a [l27576] pressing.\n\nCatalog numbers:\nOn spine: 9 60774-1\nOn label: 60774-1\n\n[On back cover]:\nElektra/Asylum Records, A Division of Warner Communications Inc.\n℗ © 1988 Elektra/Asylum Records for the United States and WEA International Inc. for the world outside of the United States.\nPrinted in U.S.A.\n\n[On inner sleeve]:\nA1, A5: © 1982 SBK April Music Inc./Purple Rabbit Music\nA4, B4: © 1983 SBK April Music Inc./Purple Rabbit Music\nA3: © 1985 SBK April Music Inc./Purple Rabbit Music\nB2, B3, B5, B6: © 1986 SBK April Music Inc./Purple Rabbit Music\nA2, B1: © 1987 SBK April Music Inc./Purple Rabbit Music\n\nDigitally recorded and mixed at Powertrax, Hollywood, CA\nThis album is dedicated to Aneta.\n\nRunout info:\n- Runouts are hand-etched\n- Variant 4 (side A): an \"s\" appears over the last M in \"DMM\"\n- Variant 7 (side B): \"1\" has been hand-scribed over \"2\" after \"DMM-\"\n- Variant 8 (both sides): \"2\" has been etched over \"1\" after \"DMM-\"",
